---
title: Migration Guide
id: migration
order: 1
description: "Migrate existing TanStack AI code to the latest version — adapter function splits, flattened options, renamed modelOptions, and the old embedding() API's replacement by embed()."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - migration
  - upgrade
  - breaking changes
  - tree-shaking
  - modelOptions
  - toServerSentEventsStream
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This guide helps you migrate from the previous version of TanStack AI to the latest version. The major changes focus on improved tree-shaking, clearer API naming, and simplified configuration."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"overview-of-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Overview of Changes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The main breaking changes in this release are:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapter functions split"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Adapters are now split into activity-specific functions for optimal tree-shaking"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common options flattened"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Options are now flattened in the config instead of nested"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"providerOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" renamed"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Now called "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" for clarity"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toResponseStream"},{"type":"text","value":" renamed"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Now called "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toServerSentEventsStream"},{"type":"text","value":" for clarity"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Embeddings removed, then reintroduced"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - The old "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"embedding()"},{"type":"text","value":" API was removed; embeddings are back as the new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"embed()"},{"type":"text","value":" activity with multimodal support"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider tools moved to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Import provider tools from each adapter's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/tools"},{"type":"text","value":" subpath"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stream: false"},{"type":"text","value":" returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ text, chunks }"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ stream: false })"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"streamToText()"},{"type":"text","value":" resolve to an object, not a string"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-adapter-functions-split","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Adapter Functions Split"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapters have been split into activity-specific functions to enable optimal tree-shaking. Instead of importing a monolithic adapter, you now import specific functions for each activity type."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"before","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openai } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openai(),\n  model: 'gpt-5.2',\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello!' }],\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"after","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello!' }],\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"key-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Key Changes"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model is passed to adapter factory"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - The model name is now passed directly to the adapter function (e.g., "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiText('gpt-5.2')"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No separate "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - The model is stored on the adapter, so you don't need to pass it separately to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Activity-specific imports"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Import only what you need (e.g., "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiText"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiSummarize"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiImage"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"all-adapter-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All Adapter Functions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each provider package now exports activity-specific functions:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"openai","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  openaiText,          // Chat/text generation\n  openaiSummarize,     // Summarization\n  openaiImage,         // Image generation\n  openaiSpeech,        // Text-to-speech\n  openaiTranscription, // Audio transcription\n  openaiVideo,         // Video generation\n} from '@tanstack/ai-openai'","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"anthropic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anthropic"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  anthropicText,       // Chat/text generation\n  anthropicSummarize,  // Summarization\n} from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"gemini","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  geminiText,       // Chat/text generation\n  geminiSummarize,  // Summarization\n  geminiImage,      // Image generation\n  geminiSpeech,     // Text-to-speech (experimental)\n} from '@tanstack/ai-gemini'","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"ollama","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ollama"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  ollamaText,       // Chat/text generation\n  ollamaSummarize,  // Summarization\n} from '@tanstack/ai-ollama'","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"migration-example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migration Example"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here's a complete example of migrating adapter usage:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"before-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openai } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { anthropic } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\n\ntype Provider = 'openai' | 'anthropic'\n\nfunction getAdapter(provider: Provider) {\n  switch (provider) {\n    case 'openai':\n      return openai()\n    case 'anthropic':\n      return anthropic()\n  }\n}\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: getAdapter(provider),\n  model: provider === 'openai' ? 'gpt-5.2' : 'claude-sonnet-4-5',\n  messages,\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"after-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\n\ntype Provider = 'openai' | 'anthropic'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello!' }]\n\nconst adapters = {\n  openai: () => openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n  anthropic: () => anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n}\n\nconst provider: Provider = 'openai'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: adapters[provider](),\n  messages,\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-common-options-flattened","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Common Options Flattened"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common options that were previously nested in an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":" object are now flattened directly in the config."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"before-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const stream = chat({\n  adapter: openai(),\n  model: 'gpt-5.2',\n  messages,\n  options: {\n    temperature: 0.7,\n    maxTokens: 1000,\n    topP: 0.9,\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"after-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n  messages,\n  temperature: 0.7,\n  maxTokens: 1000,\n  topP: 0.9,\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"available-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These options are now available at the top level:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"},{"type":"text","value":" - Controls randomness (0.0 to 2.0)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"topP"},{"type":"text","value":" - Nucleus sampling parameter"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTokens"},{"type":"text","value":" - Maximum tokens to generate"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"},{"type":"text","value":" - Additional metadata to attach"}]}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Heads up — sampling has since moved (breaking)."}]},{"type":"text","value":" In a later release, the sampling props ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"topP"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTokens"},{"type":"text","value":") were removed from the root of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" and now live in provider-native "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":". Passing them at the root no longer type-checks or takes effect. See "},{"type":"link","href":"./sampling-options-to-model-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the codemod and provider-native key names. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"},{"type":"text","value":" stays at the root."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"3-provideroptions-modeloptions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"providerOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"providerOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter has been renamed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" for clarity. This parameter contains model-specific options that vary by provider and model."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"before-4","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const stream = chat({\n  adapter: openai(),\n  model: 'gpt-5.2',\n  messages,\n  providerOptions: {\n    // OpenAI-specific options\n    responseFormat: { type: 'json_object' },\n    logitBias: { '123': 1.0 },\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"after-4","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    // OpenAI-specific options\n    responseFormat: { type: 'json_object' },\n    logitBias: { '123': 1.0 },\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"type-safety","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Safety"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" is fully typed based on the adapter and model you're using:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst adapter = openaiText('gpt-5.2')\n\n// TypeScript knows the exact modelOptions type for gpt-5.2\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter,\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    // Autocomplete and type checking for gpt-5.2 options\n    responseFormat: { type: 'json_object' },\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"4-toresponsestream-toserversenteventsstream","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toResponseStream"},{"type":"text","value":" → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toServerSentEventsStream"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toResponseStream"},{"type":"text","value":" function has been renamed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toServerSentEventsStream"},{"type":"text","value":" to better reflect its purpose. Additionally, the API has changed slightly."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"before-5","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toResponseStream } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openai } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n  const abortController = new AbortController()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openai(),\n    model: 'gpt-5.2',\n    messages,\n    abortController,\n  })\n\n  return toResponseStream(stream, { abortController })\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"after-5","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsStream } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n  const abortController = new AbortController()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n    messages,\n    abortController,\n  })\n\n  const readableStream = toServerSentEventsStream(stream, abortController)\n  return new Response(readableStream, {\n    headers: {\n      'Content-Type': 'text/event-stream',\n      'Cache-Control': 'no-cache',\n      Connection: 'keep-alive',\n    },\n  })\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"key-changes-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Key Changes"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Function renamed"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toResponseStream"},{"type":"text","value":" → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toServerSentEventsStream"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns ReadableStream"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Now returns a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReadableStream"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manual Response creation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - You create the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response"},{"type":"text","value":" object yourself with appropriate headers"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AbortController parameter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Passed as a separate parameter instead of in options"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"alternative-http-stream-format","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alternative: HTTP Stream Format"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you need HTTP stream format (newline-delimited JSON) instead of SSE, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toHttpStream"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { toHttpStream } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst readableStream = toHttpStream(stream, abortController)\nreturn new Response(readableStream, {\n  headers: {\n    'Content-Type': 'application/x-ndjson',\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"5-embeddings-removed-then-reintroduced-as-embed","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5. Embeddings Removed, Then Reintroduced as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"embed()"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The original "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"embedding()"},{"type":"text","value":" function was removed from TanStack AI. Embeddings have since returned as a new activity with a different API: a single "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"embed()"},{"type":"text","value":" function with multimodal input support and per-model type safety. The old "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"embedding()"},{"type":"text","value":" name and adapter factories (like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiEmbed()"},{"type":"text","value":") are not coming back."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"before-6","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { embedding } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiEmbed } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst result = await embedding({\n  adapter: openaiEmbed(),\n  model: 'text-embedding-3-small',\n  input: 'Hello, world!',\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"after-6","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { embed } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiEmbedding } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: openaiEmbedding('text-embedding-3-small'),\n  input: 'Hello, world!',\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.embeddings[0]?.vector)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Key differences from the old API:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model moves into the adapter factory"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiEmbedding('text-embedding-3-small')"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of a separate "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model"},{"type":"text","value":" option, matching every other activity"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Single function for one or many inputs"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts a single item or an array; the result always has an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"embeddings"},{"type":"text","value":" array with one vector per input item"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Multimodal inputs"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - models like Cohere embed-v4.0 and Amazon Titan Multimodal accept image parts and fused text+image items"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Top-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dimensions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - request Matryoshka dimensions without provider-specific options"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../embeddings.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Embeddings guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for full usage."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"6-provider-tools-moved-to-tools-subpath","children":[{"type":"text","value":"6. Provider Tools Moved to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/tools"},{"type":"text","value":" Subpath"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider-specific tools (web search, code execution, computer use, etc.) are now\nexported from a dedicated "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/tools"},{"type":"text","value":" subpath on every adapter package. This keeps\ntool imports tree-shakeable and avoids name collisions between providers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The only breaking change is in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-openrouter"},{"type":"text","value":":\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createWebSearchTool"},{"type":"text","value":" has been removed from the package root, renamed to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"webSearchTool"},{"type":"text","value":", and moved to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-openrouter/tools"},{"type":"text","value":". Every other\nprovider tool (Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini) is newly exported — no existing\nimport breaks."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"before-7","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createWebSearchTool } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter'\n\nconst tools = [\n  createWebSearchTool({ engine: 'native', maxResults: 5 }),\n]","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"after-7","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { webSearchTool } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/tools'\n\nconst tools = [\n  webSearchTool({ engine: 'native', maxResults: 5 }),\n]","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"key-changes-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Key Changes"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import path is now "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — matches the existing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/adapters"},{"type":"text","value":" subpath\npattern used elsewhere in each provider package."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Factory renamed"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createWebSearchTool"},{"type":"text","value":" → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"webSearchTool"},{"type":"text","value":". The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"create*"},{"type":"text","value":"\nprefix has been dropped to align with every other provider\n("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"webSearchTool"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools"},{"type":"text","value":", etc.)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime behavior is unchanged"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — the factory accepts the same config\nobject and returns a tool that works identically in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ tools: [...] })"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type-level gating is new"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — if you pass a provider tool to a model that\ndoesn't support it (per the model's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"supports.tools"},{"type":"text","value":" array), you now get a\ntype error on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":" array. User-defined "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolDefinition()"},{"type":"text","value":" tools are\nunaffected."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For the full list of available provider tools and which models support each\none, see "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/provider-tools.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"7-stream-false-returns-text-chunks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"7. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stream: false"},{"type":"text","value":" Returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ text, chunks }"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ stream: false })"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"streamToText(stream)"},{"type":"text","value":" now resolve to a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatResult"},{"type":"text","value":" object, not a string. Take "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"},{"type":"text","value":" from the result."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"before-8","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, streamToText } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst text = await chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.6'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello!' }],\n  stream: false,\n})\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.6'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello!' }],\n})\nconst streamedText = await streamToText(stream)","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"after-8","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, streamToText } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst { text } = await chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.6'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello!' }],\n  stream: false,\n})\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.6'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello!' }],\n})\nconst { text: streamedText } = await streamToText(stream)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"},{"type":"text","value":" is the same string as before. The new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunks"},{"type":"text","value":" array holds every chunk of the run, so you can also read tool calls, usage, and interrupts. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../api/ai.md#returns","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stream: false"},{"type":"text","value":" still resolves to the parsed object."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"complete-migration-example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Complete Migration Example"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here's a complete example showing all the changes together:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"before-9","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toResponseStream } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openai } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n  const abortController = new AbortController()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openai(),\n    model: 'gpt-5.2',\n    messages,\n    options: {\n      temperature: 0.7,\n      maxTokens: 1000,\n    },\n    providerOptions: {\n      responseFormat: { type: 'json_object' },\n    },\n    abortController,\n  })\n\n  return toResponseStream(stream, { abortController })\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"after-9","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsStream } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n  const abortController = new AbortController()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n    messages,\n    // Sampling now lives in provider-native `modelOptions` (OpenAI Responses\n    // keys: `temperature`, `max_output_tokens`). `metadata` stays at the root.\n    modelOptions: {\n      temperature: 0.7,\n      max_output_tokens: 1000,\n      responseFormat: { type: 'json_object' },\n    },\n    abortController,\n  })\n\n  const readableStream = toServerSentEventsStream(stream, abortController)\n  return new Response(readableStream, {\n    headers: {\n      'Content-Type': 'text/event-stream',\n      'Cache-Control': 'no-cache',\n      Connection: 'keep-alive',\n    },\n  })\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"benefits-of-these-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Benefits of These Changes"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Better Tree-Shaking"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Import only what you need, resulting in smaller bundle sizes"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clearer API"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Function names clearly indicate their purpose"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Safety"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Model-specific options are fully typed"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Simpler Configuration"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Flattened options are easier to work with"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focused Scope"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Removed features that are better handled elsewhere"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"need-help","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Need Help?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you encounter issues during migration:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check the "},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/tree-shaking","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tree-Shaking Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for details on the new adapter structure"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Review the "},{"type":"link","href":"../api/ai","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API Reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for complete function signatures"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Look at the "},{"type":"link","href":"../getting-started/quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"examples"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for working code samples"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"overview-of-changes","text":"Overview of Changes","level":2},{"id":"1-adapter-functions-split","text":"1. Adapter Functions Split","level":2},{"id":"before","text":"Before","level":3},{"id":"after","text":"After","level":3},{"id":"key-changes","text":"Key Changes","level":3},{"id":"all-adapter-functions","text":"All Adapter Functions","level":3},{"id":"openai","text":"OpenAI","level":4},{"id":"anthropic","text":"Anthropic","level":4},{"id":"gemini","text":"Gemini","level":4},{"id":"ollama","text":"Ollama","level":4},{"id":"migration-example","text":"Migration Example","level":3},{"id":"before-2","text":"Before","level":4},{"id":"after-2","text":"After","level":4},{"id":"2-common-options-flattened","text":"2. Common Options Flattened","level":2},{"id":"before-3","text":"Before","level":3},{"id":"after-3","text":"After","level":3},{"id":"available-options","text":"Available Options","level":3},{"id":"3-provideroptions-modeloptions","text":"3. providerOptions → modelOptions","level":2},{"id":"before-4","text":"Before","level":3},{"id":"after-4","text":"After","level":3},{"id":"type-safety","text":"Type Safety","level":3},{"id":"4-toresponsestream-toserversenteventsstream","text":"4. toResponseStream → toServerSentEventsStream","level":2},{"id":"before-5","text":"Before","level":3},{"id":"after-5","text":"After","level":3},{"id":"key-changes-2","text":"Key Changes","level":3},{"id":"alternative-http-stream-format","text":"Alternative: HTTP Stream Format","level":3},{"id":"5-embeddings-removed-then-reintroduced-as-embed","text":"5. Embeddings Removed, Then Reintroduced as embed()","level":2},{"id":"before-6","text":"Before","level":3},{"id":"after-6","text":"After","level":3},{"id":"6-provider-tools-moved-to-tools-subpath","text":"6. Provider Tools Moved to /tools Subpath","level":2},{"id":"before-7","text":"Before","level":3},{"id":"after-7","text":"After","level":3},{"id":"key-changes-3","text":"Key Changes","level":3},{"id":"7-stream-false-returns-text-chunks","text":"7. stream: false Returns { text, chunks }","level":2},{"id":"before-8","text":"Before","level":3},{"id":"after-8","text":"After","level":3},{"id":"complete-migration-example","text":"Complete Migration Example","level":2},{"id":"before-9","text":"Before","level":3},{"id":"after-9","text":"After","level":3},{"id":"benefits-of-these-changes","text":"Benefits of These Changes","level":2},{"id":"need-help","text":"Need Help?","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThis guide helps you migrate from the previous version of TanStack AI to the latest version. The major changes focus on improved tree-shaking, clearer API naming, and simplified configuration.\n\n## Overview of Changes\n\nThe main breaking changes in this release are:\n\n1. **Adapter functions split** - Adapters are now split into activity-specific functions for optimal tree-shaking\n2. **Common options flattened** - Options are now flattened in the config instead of nested\n3. **`providerOptions` renamed** - Now called `modelOptions` for clarity\n4. **`toResponseStream` renamed** - Now called `toServerSentEventsStream` for clarity\n5. **Embeddings removed, then reintroduced** - The old `embedding()` API was removed; embeddings are back as the new `embed()` activity with multimodal support\n6. **Provider tools moved to `/tools`** - Import provider tools from each adapter's `/tools` subpath\n7. **`stream: false` returns `{ text, chunks }`** - `chat({ stream: false })` and `streamToText()` resolve to an object, not a string\n\n## 1. Adapter Functions Split\n\nAdapters have been split into activity-specific functions to enable optimal tree-shaking. Instead of importing a monolithic adapter, you now import specific functions for each activity type.\n\n### Before\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openai } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openai(),\n  model: 'gpt-5.2',\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello!' }],\n})\n```\n\n### After\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello!' }],\n})\n```\n\n### Key Changes\n\n- **Model is passed to adapter factory** - The model name is now passed directly to the adapter function (e.g., `openaiText('gpt-5.2')`)\n- **No separate `model` parameter** - The model is stored on the adapter, so you don't need to pass it separately to `chat()`\n- **Activity-specific imports** - Import only what you need (e.g., `openaiText`, `openaiSummarize`, `openaiImage`)\n\n### All Adapter Functions\n\nEach provider package now exports activity-specific functions:\n\n#### OpenAI\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  openaiText,          // Chat/text generation\n  openaiSummarize,     // Summarization\n  openaiImage,         // Image generation\n  openaiSpeech,        // Text-to-speech\n  openaiTranscription, // Audio transcription\n  openaiVideo,         // Video generation\n} from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n```\n\n#### Anthropic\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  anthropicText,       // Chat/text generation\n  anthropicSummarize,  // Summarization\n} from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\n```\n\n#### Gemini\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  geminiText,       // Chat/text generation\n  geminiSummarize,  // Summarization\n  geminiImage,      // Image generation\n  geminiSpeech,     // Text-to-speech (experimental)\n} from '@tanstack/ai-gemini'\n```\n\n#### Ollama\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  ollamaText,       // Chat/text generation\n  ollamaSummarize,  // Summarization\n} from '@tanstack/ai-ollama'\n```\n\n### Migration Example\n\nHere's a complete example of migrating adapter usage:\n\n#### Before\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openai } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { anthropic } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\n\ntype Provider = 'openai' | 'anthropic'\n\nfunction getAdapter(provider: Provider) {\n  switch (provider) {\n    case 'openai':\n      return openai()\n    case 'anthropic':\n      return anthropic()\n  }\n}\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: getAdapter(provider),\n  model: provider === 'openai' ? 'gpt-5.2' : 'claude-sonnet-4-5',\n  messages,\n})\n```\n\n#### After\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\n\ntype Provider = 'openai' | 'anthropic'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello!' }]\n\nconst adapters = {\n  openai: () => openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n  anthropic: () => anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n}\n\nconst provider: Provider = 'openai'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: adapters[provider](),\n  messages,\n})\n```\n\n## 2. Common Options Flattened\n\nCommon options that were previously nested in an `options` object are now flattened directly in the config.\n\n### Before\n\n```typescript ignore\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openai(),\n  model: 'gpt-5.2',\n  messages,\n  options: {\n    temperature: 0.7,\n    maxTokens: 1000,\n    topP: 0.9,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### After\n\n```typescript ignore\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n  messages,\n  temperature: 0.7,\n  maxTokens: 1000,\n  topP: 0.9,\n})\n```\n\n### Available Options\n\nThese options are now available at the top level:\n\n- `temperature` - Controls randomness (0.0 to 2.0)\n- `topP` - Nucleus sampling parameter\n- `maxTokens` - Maximum tokens to generate\n- `metadata` - Additional metadata to attach\n\n> **Heads up — sampling has since moved (breaking).** In a later release, the sampling props (`temperature`, `topP`, `maxTokens`) were removed from the root of `chat()` and now live in provider-native `modelOptions`. Passing them at the root no longer type-checks or takes effect. See [Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions](./sampling-options-to-model-options) for the codemod and provider-native key names. `metadata` stays at the root.\n\n## 3. `providerOptions` → `modelOptions`\n\nThe `providerOptions` parameter has been renamed to `modelOptions` for clarity. This parameter contains model-specific options that vary by provider and model.\n\n### Before\n\n```typescript ignore\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openai(),\n  model: 'gpt-5.2',\n  messages,\n  providerOptions: {\n    // OpenAI-specific options\n    responseFormat: { type: 'json_object' },\n    logitBias: { '123': 1.0 },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### After\n\n```typescript ignore\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    // OpenAI-specific options\n    responseFormat: { type: 'json_object' },\n    logitBias: { '123': 1.0 },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Type Safety\n\n`modelOptions` is fully typed based on the adapter and model you're using:\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst adapter = openaiText('gpt-5.2')\n\n// TypeScript knows the exact modelOptions type for gpt-5.2\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter,\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    // Autocomplete and type checking for gpt-5.2 options\n    responseFormat: { type: 'json_object' },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## 4. `toResponseStream` → `toServerSentEventsStream`\n\nThe `toResponseStream` function has been renamed to `toServerSentEventsStream` to better reflect its purpose. Additionally, the API has changed slightly.\n\n### Before\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { chat, toResponseStream } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openai } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n  const abortController = new AbortController()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openai(),\n    model: 'gpt-5.2',\n    messages,\n    abortController,\n  })\n\n  return toResponseStream(stream, { abortController })\n}\n```\n\n### After\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsStream } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n  const abortController = new AbortController()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n    messages,\n    abortController,\n  })\n\n  const readableStream = toServerSentEventsStream(stream, abortController)\n  return new Response(readableStream, {\n    headers: {\n      'Content-Type': 'text/event-stream',\n      'Cache-Control': 'no-cache',\n      Connection: 'keep-alive',\n    },\n  })\n}\n```\n\n### Key Changes\n\n- **Function renamed** - `toResponseStream` → `toServerSentEventsStream`\n- **Returns ReadableStream** - Now returns a `ReadableStream` instead of a `Response`\n- **Manual Response creation** - You create the `Response` object yourself with appropriate headers\n- **AbortController parameter** - Passed as a separate parameter instead of in options\n\n### Alternative: HTTP Stream Format\n\nIf you need HTTP stream format (newline-delimited JSON) instead of SSE, use `toHttpStream`:\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { toHttpStream } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst readableStream = toHttpStream(stream, abortController)\nreturn new Response(readableStream, {\n  headers: {\n    'Content-Type': 'application/x-ndjson',\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## 5. Embeddings Removed, Then Reintroduced as `embed()`\n\nThe original `embedding()` function was removed from TanStack AI. Embeddings have since returned as a new activity with a different API: a single `embed()` function with multimodal input support and per-model type safety. The old `embedding()` name and adapter factories (like `openaiEmbed()`) are not coming back.\n\n### Before\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { embedding } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiEmbed } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst result = await embedding({\n  adapter: openaiEmbed(),\n  model: 'text-embedding-3-small',\n  input: 'Hello, world!',\n})\n```\n\n### After\n\n```typescript\nimport { embed } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiEmbedding } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: openaiEmbedding('text-embedding-3-small'),\n  input: 'Hello, world!',\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.embeddings[0]?.vector)\n```\n\nKey differences from the old API:\n\n- **Model moves into the adapter factory** - `openaiEmbedding('text-embedding-3-small')` instead of a separate `model` option, matching every other activity\n- **Single function for one or many inputs** - `input` accepts a single item or an array; the result always has an `embeddings` array with one vector per input item\n- **Multimodal inputs** - models like Cohere embed-v4.0 and Amazon Titan Multimodal accept image parts and fused text+image items\n- **Top-level `dimensions`** - request Matryoshka dimensions without provider-specific options\n\nSee the [Embeddings guide](../embeddings.md) for full usage.\n\n## 6. Provider Tools Moved to `/tools` Subpath\n\nProvider-specific tools (web search, code execution, computer use, etc.) are now\nexported from a dedicated `/tools` subpath on every adapter package. This keeps\ntool imports tree-shakeable and avoids name collisions between providers.\n\nThe only breaking change is in `@tanstack/ai-openrouter`:\n`createWebSearchTool` has been removed from the package root, renamed to\n`webSearchTool`, and moved to `@tanstack/ai-openrouter/tools`. Every other\nprovider tool (Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini) is newly exported — no existing\nimport breaks.\n\n### Before\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { createWebSearchTool } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter'\n\nconst tools = [\n  createWebSearchTool({ engine: 'native', maxResults: 5 }),\n]\n```\n\n### After\n\n```typescript\nimport { webSearchTool } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/tools'\n\nconst tools = [\n  webSearchTool({ engine: 'native', maxResults: 5 }),\n]\n```\n\n### Key Changes\n\n- **Import path is now `/tools`** — matches the existing `/adapters` subpath\n  pattern used elsewhere in each provider package.\n- **Factory renamed** — `createWebSearchTool` → `webSearchTool`. The `create*`\n  prefix has been dropped to align with every other provider\n  (`webSearchTool` in `@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools`,\n  `@tanstack/ai-openai/tools`, etc.).\n- **Runtime behavior is unchanged** — the factory accepts the same config\n  object and returns a tool that works identically in `chat({ tools: [...] })`.\n- **Type-level gating is new** — if you pass a provider tool to a model that\n  doesn't support it (per the model's `supports.tools` array), you now get a\n  type error on the `tools` array. User-defined `toolDefinition()` tools are\n  unaffected.\n\nFor the full list of available provider tools and which models support each\none, see [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md).\n\n## 7. `stream: false` Returns `{ text, chunks }`\n\n`chat({ stream: false })` and `streamToText(stream)` now resolve to a `ChatResult` object, not a string. Take `text` from the result.\n\n### Before\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { chat, streamToText } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst text = await chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.6'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello!' }],\n  stream: false,\n})\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.6'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello!' }],\n})\nconst streamedText = await streamToText(stream)\n```\n\n### After\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, streamToText } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst { text } = await chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.6'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello!' }],\n  stream: false,\n})\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.6'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello!' }],\n})\nconst { text: streamedText } = await streamToText(stream)\n```\n\n`text` is the same string as before. The new `chunks` array holds every chunk of the run, so you can also read tool calls, usage, and interrupts. See [`chat()` returns](../api/ai.md#returns).\n\nWith `outputSchema`, `stream: false` still resolves to the parsed object.\n\n## Complete Migration Example\n\nHere's a complete example showing all the changes together:\n\n### Before\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { chat, toResponseStream } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openai } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n  const abortController = new AbortController()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openai(),\n    model: 'gpt-5.2',\n    messages,\n    options: {\n      temperature: 0.7,\n      maxTokens: 1000,\n    },\n    providerOptions: {\n      responseFormat: { type: 'json_object' },\n    },\n    abortController,\n  })\n\n  return toResponseStream(stream, { abortController })\n}\n```\n\n### After\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsStream } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n  const abortController = new AbortController()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n    messages,\n    // Sampling now lives in provider-native `modelOptions` (OpenAI Responses\n    // keys: `temperature`, `max_output_tokens`). `metadata` stays at the root.\n    modelOptions: {\n      temperature: 0.7,\n      max_output_tokens: 1000,\n      responseFormat: { type: 'json_object' },\n    },\n    abortController,\n  })\n\n  const readableStream = toServerSentEventsStream(stream, abortController)\n  return new Response(readableStream, {\n    headers: {\n      'Content-Type': 'text/event-stream',\n      'Cache-Control': 'no-cache',\n      Connection: 'keep-alive',\n    },\n  })\n}\n```\n\n## Benefits of These Changes\n\n1. **Better Tree-Shaking** - Import only what you need, resulting in smaller bundle sizes\n2. **Clearer API** - Function names clearly indicate their purpose\n3. **Type Safety** - Model-specific options are fully typed\n4. **Simpler Configuration** - Flattened options are easier to work with\n5. **Focused Scope** - Removed features that are better handled elsewhere\n\n## Need Help?\n\nIf you encounter issues during migration:\n\n1. Check the [Tree-Shaking Guide](../advanced/tree-shaking) for details on the new adapter structure\n2. Review the [API Reference](../api/ai) for complete function signatures\n3. Look at the [examples](../getting-started/quick-start) for working code samples\n\n\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Migration Guide\nid: migration\norder: 1\ndescription: \"Migrate existing TanStack AI code to the latest version — adapter function splits, flattened options, renamed modelOptions, and the old embedding() API's replacement by embed().\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - migration\n  - upgrade\n  - breaking changes\n  - tree-shaking\n  - modelOptions\n  - toServerSentEventsStream\n---\n\nThis guide helps you migrate from the previous version of TanStack AI to the latest version. The major changes focus on improved tree-shaking, clearer API naming, and simplified configuration.\n\n## Overview of Changes\n\nThe main breaking changes in this release are:\n\n1. **Adapter functions split** - Adapters are now split into activity-specific functions for optimal tree-shaking\n2. **Common options flattened** - Options are now flattened in the config instead of nested\n3. **`providerOptions` renamed** - Now called `modelOptions` for clarity\n4. **`toResponseStream` renamed** - Now called `toServerSentEventsStream` for clarity\n5. **Embeddings removed, then reintroduced** - The old `embedding()` API was removed; embeddings are back as the new `embed()` activity with multimodal support\n6. **Provider tools moved to `/tools`** - Import provider tools from each adapter's `/tools` subpath\n7. **`stream: false` returns `{ text, chunks }`** - `chat({ stream: false })` and `streamToText()` resolve to an object, not a string\n\n## 1. Adapter Functions Split\n\nAdapters have been split into activity-specific functions to enable optimal tree-shaking. Instead of importing a monolithic adapter, you now import specific functions for each activity type.\n\n### Before\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openai } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openai(),\n  model: 'gpt-5.2',\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello!' }],\n})\n```\n\n### After\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello!' }],\n})\n```\n\n### Key Changes\n\n- **Model is passed to adapter factory** - The model name is now passed directly to the adapter function (e.g., `openaiText('gpt-5.2')`)\n- **No separate `model` parameter** - The model is stored on the adapter, so you don't need to pass it separately to `chat()`\n- **Activity-specific imports** - Import only what you need (e.g., `openaiText`, `openaiSummarize`, `openaiImage`)\n\n### All Adapter Functions\n\nEach provider package now exports activity-specific functions:\n\n#### OpenAI\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  openaiText,          // Chat/text generation\n  openaiSummarize,     // Summarization\n  openaiImage,         // Image generation\n  openaiSpeech,        // Text-to-speech\n  openaiTranscription, // Audio transcription\n  openaiVideo,         // Video generation\n} from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n```\n\n#### Anthropic\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  anthropicText,       // Chat/text generation\n  anthropicSummarize,  // Summarization\n} from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\n```\n\n#### Gemini\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  geminiText,       // Chat/text generation\n  geminiSummarize,  // Summarization\n  geminiImage,      // Image generation\n  geminiSpeech,     // Text-to-speech (experimental)\n} from '@tanstack/ai-gemini'\n```\n\n#### Ollama\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  ollamaText,       // Chat/text generation\n  ollamaSummarize,  // Summarization\n} from '@tanstack/ai-ollama'\n```\n\n### Migration Example\n\nHere's a complete example of migrating adapter usage:\n\n#### Before\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openai } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { anthropic } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\n\ntype Provider = 'openai' | 'anthropic'\n\nfunction getAdapter(provider: Provider) {\n  switch (provider) {\n    case 'openai':\n      return openai()\n    case 'anthropic':\n      return anthropic()\n  }\n}\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: getAdapter(provider),\n  model: provider === 'openai' ? 'gpt-5.2' : 'claude-sonnet-4-5',\n  messages,\n})\n```\n\n#### After\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\n\ntype Provider = 'openai' | 'anthropic'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello!' }]\n\nconst adapters = {\n  openai: () => openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n  anthropic: () => anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n}\n\nconst provider: Provider = 'openai'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: adapters[provider](),\n  messages,\n})\n```\n\n## 2. Common Options Flattened\n\nCommon options that were previously nested in an `options` object are now flattened directly in the config.\n\n### Before\n\n```typescript ignore\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openai(),\n  model: 'gpt-5.2',\n  messages,\n  options: {\n    temperature: 0.7,\n    maxTokens: 1000,\n    topP: 0.9,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### After\n\n```typescript ignore\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n  messages,\n  temperature: 0.7,\n  maxTokens: 1000,\n  topP: 0.9,\n})\n```\n\n### Available Options\n\nThese options are now available at the top level:\n\n- `temperature` - Controls randomness (0.0 to 2.0)\n- `topP` - Nucleus sampling parameter\n- `maxTokens` - Maximum tokens to generate\n- `metadata` - Additional metadata to attach\n\n> **Heads up — sampling has since moved (breaking).** In a later release, the sampling props (`temperature`, `topP`, `maxTokens`) were removed from the root of `chat()` and now live in provider-native `modelOptions`. Passing them at the root no longer type-checks or takes effect. See [Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions](./sampling-options-to-model-options) for the codemod and provider-native key names. `metadata` stays at the root.\n\n## 3. `providerOptions` → `modelOptions`\n\nThe `providerOptions` parameter has been renamed to `modelOptions` for clarity. This parameter contains model-specific options that vary by provider and model.\n\n### Before\n\n```typescript ignore\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openai(),\n  model: 'gpt-5.2',\n  messages,\n  providerOptions: {\n    // OpenAI-specific options\n    responseFormat: { type: 'json_object' },\n    logitBias: { '123': 1.0 },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### After\n\n```typescript ignore\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    // OpenAI-specific options\n    responseFormat: { type: 'json_object' },\n    logitBias: { '123': 1.0 },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Type Safety\n\n`modelOptions` is fully typed based on the adapter and model you're using:\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst adapter = openaiText('gpt-5.2')\n\n// TypeScript knows the exact modelOptions type for gpt-5.2\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter,\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    // Autocomplete and type checking for gpt-5.2 options\n    responseFormat: { type: 'json_object' },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## 4. `toResponseStream` → `toServerSentEventsStream`\n\nThe `toResponseStream` function has been renamed to `toServerSentEventsStream` to better reflect its purpose. Additionally, the API has changed slightly.\n\n### Before\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { chat, toResponseStream } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openai } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n  const abortController = new AbortController()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openai(),\n    model: 'gpt-5.2',\n    messages,\n    abortController,\n  })\n\n  return toResponseStream(stream, { abortController })\n}\n```\n\n### After\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsStream } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n  const abortController = new AbortController()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n    messages,\n    abortController,\n  })\n\n  const readableStream = toServerSentEventsStream(stream, abortController)\n  return new Response(readableStream, {\n    headers: {\n      'Content-Type': 'text/event-stream',\n      'Cache-Control': 'no-cache',\n      Connection: 'keep-alive',\n    },\n  })\n}\n```\n\n### Key Changes\n\n- **Function renamed** - `toResponseStream` → `toServerSentEventsStream`\n- **Returns ReadableStream** - Now returns a `ReadableStream` instead of a `Response`\n- **Manual Response creation** - You create the `Response` object yourself with appropriate headers\n- **AbortController parameter** - Passed as a separate parameter instead of in options\n\n### Alternative: HTTP Stream Format\n\nIf you need HTTP stream format (newline-delimited JSON) instead of SSE, use `toHttpStream`:\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { toHttpStream } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst readableStream = toHttpStream(stream, abortController)\nreturn new Response(readableStream, {\n  headers: {\n    'Content-Type': 'application/x-ndjson',\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## 5. Embeddings Removed, Then Reintroduced as `embed()`\n\nThe original `embedding()` function was removed from TanStack AI. Embeddings have since returned as a new activity with a different API: a single `embed()` function with multimodal input support and per-model type safety. The old `embedding()` name and adapter factories (like `openaiEmbed()`) are not coming back.\n\n### Before\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { embedding } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiEmbed } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst result = await embedding({\n  adapter: openaiEmbed(),\n  model: 'text-embedding-3-small',\n  input: 'Hello, world!',\n})\n```\n\n### After\n\n```typescript\nimport { embed } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiEmbedding } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: openaiEmbedding('text-embedding-3-small'),\n  input: 'Hello, world!',\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.embeddings[0]?.vector)\n```\n\nKey differences from the old API:\n\n- **Model moves into the adapter factory** - `openaiEmbedding('text-embedding-3-small')` instead of a separate `model` option, matching every other activity\n- **Single function for one or many inputs** - `input` accepts a single item or an array; the result always has an `embeddings` array with one vector per input item\n- **Multimodal inputs** - models like Cohere embed-v4.0 and Amazon Titan Multimodal accept image parts and fused text+image items\n- **Top-level `dimensions`** - request Matryoshka dimensions without provider-specific options\n\nSee the [Embeddings guide](../embeddings.md) for full usage.\n\n## 6. Provider Tools Moved to `/tools` Subpath\n\nProvider-specific tools (web search, code execution, computer use, etc.) are now\nexported from a dedicated `/tools` subpath on every adapter package. This keeps\ntool imports tree-shakeable and avoids name collisions between providers.\n\nThe only breaking change is in `@tanstack/ai-openrouter`:\n`createWebSearchTool` has been removed from the package root, renamed to\n`webSearchTool`, and moved to `@tanstack/ai-openrouter/tools`. Every other\nprovider tool (Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini) is newly exported — no existing\nimport breaks.\n\n### Before\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { createWebSearchTool } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter'\n\nconst tools = [\n  createWebSearchTool({ engine: 'native', maxResults: 5 }),\n]\n```\n\n### After\n\n```typescript\nimport { webSearchTool } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/tools'\n\nconst tools = [\n  webSearchTool({ engine: 'native', maxResults: 5 }),\n]\n```\n\n### Key Changes\n\n- **Import path is now `/tools`** — matches the existing `/adapters` subpath\n  pattern used elsewhere in each provider package.\n- **Factory renamed** — `createWebSearchTool` → `webSearchTool`. The `create*`\n  prefix has been dropped to align with every other provider\n  (`webSearchTool` in `@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools`,\n  `@tanstack/ai-openai/tools`, etc.).\n- **Runtime behavior is unchanged** — the factory accepts the same config\n  object and returns a tool that works identically in `chat({ tools: [...] })`.\n- **Type-level gating is new** — if you pass a provider tool to a model that\n  doesn't support it (per the model's `supports.tools` array), you now get a\n  type error on the `tools` array. User-defined `toolDefinition()` tools are\n  unaffected.\n\nFor the full list of available provider tools and which models support each\none, see [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md).\n\n## 7. `stream: false` Returns `{ text, chunks }`\n\n`chat({ stream: false })` and `streamToText(stream)` now resolve to a `ChatResult` object, not a string. Take `text` from the result.\n\n### Before\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { chat, streamToText } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst text = await chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.6'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello!' }],\n  stream: false,\n})\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.6'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello!' }],\n})\nconst streamedText = await streamToText(stream)\n```\n\n### After\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, streamToText } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst { text } = await chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.6'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello!' }],\n  stream: false,\n})\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.6'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello!' }],\n})\nconst { text: streamedText } = await streamToText(stream)\n```\n\n`text` is the same string as before. The new `chunks` array holds every chunk of the run, so you can also read tool calls, usage, and interrupts. See [`chat()` returns](../api/ai.md#returns).\n\nWith `outputSchema`, `stream: false` still resolves to the parsed object.\n\n## Complete Migration Example\n\nHere's a complete example showing all the changes together:\n\n### Before\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { chat, toResponseStream } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openai } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n  const abortController = new AbortController()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openai(),\n    model: 'gpt-5.2',\n    messages,\n    options: {\n      temperature: 0.7,\n      maxTokens: 1000,\n    },\n    providerOptions: {\n      responseFormat: { type: 'json_object' },\n    },\n    abortController,\n  })\n\n  return toResponseStream(stream, { abortController })\n}\n```\n\n### After\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsStream } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n  const abortController = new AbortController()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n    messages,\n    // Sampling now lives in provider-native `modelOptions` (OpenAI Responses\n    // keys: `temperature`, `max_output_tokens`). `metadata` stays at the root.\n    modelOptions: {\n      temperature: 0.7,\n      max_output_tokens: 1000,\n      responseFormat: { type: 'json_object' },\n    },\n    abortController,\n  })\n\n  const readableStream = toServerSentEventsStream(stream, abortController)\n  return new Response(readableStream, {\n    headers: {\n      'Content-Type': 'text/event-stream',\n      'Cache-Control': 'no-cache',\n      Connection: 'keep-alive',\n    },\n  })\n}\n```\n\n## Benefits of These Changes\n\n1. **Better Tree-Shaking** - Import only what you need, resulting in smaller bundle sizes\n2. **Clearer API** - Function names clearly indicate their purpose\n3. **Type Safety** - Model-specific options are fully typed\n4. **Simpler Configuration** - Flattened options are easier to work with\n5. **Focused Scope** - Removed features that are better handled elsewhere\n\n## Need Help?\n\nIf you encounter issues during migration:\n\n1. Check the [Tree-Shaking Guide](../advanced/tree-shaking) for details on the new adapter structure\n2. Review the [API Reference](../api/ai) for complete function signatures\n3. Look at the [examples](../getting-started/quick-start) for working code samples\n\n\n"}
